# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Artifacts are added on purpose, never swept in.
#
# The three directories below hold what the study measured, and they also hold
# whatever the last run happened to leave on disk -- 653 MB of checkpoints from
# seed sweeps, 22 GB of superseded captures, results from experiments that were
# retired. Ignoring them wholesale does NOT untrack anything: a file already in
# git stays in git and its edits still show up. What it stops is `git add -A`
# quietly enlarging the published record with working output, which is how a
# repository ends up shipping results nobody chose to publish.
#
# To add a new artifact, name it: `git add -f results/<the file>`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
results/**
data/**
checkpoints/**

# The captures live on Hugging Face; scripts/fetch_captures.py puts them back.
# The training frames, about 59 GB, are regenerable and deliberately not shipped.

# Downloaded wheels. One reached a commit before this line existed.
*.whl
